  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "If $P$ is a statement, $\\text{t}$ is a tautology, and $\\text{c}$ is a contradiction, complete the following table of logical equivalences.\n\n| Statement | Is Logically Equivalent To |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{t}∧\\text{c}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{c}∨\\text{c}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{c}∧¬P$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $P∨\\text{c}$ | {{field-4}} |",
